    <briefdescription>
<para>The integer type used to compare a value of type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The primary template is the type itself. The character types (<computeroutput>char</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>wchar_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char8_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char16_t</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>char32_t</computeroutput>) are compared as the numbers that they hold, so they are replaced by the integer type of the same size and signedness, which <computeroutput>std::cmp_*()</computeroutput> accepts; the signedness of <computeroutput>char</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>wchar_t</computeroutput> depends on the platform, and is kept.</para>
